name grid_stress
describe The same worst pose as stress_pose, but with goal 256's CELL GRID on (--cell-log2 5). Kept beside stress_pose rather than replacing it so the two structures are measured at one pose, and so a regression in either is attributable. describe-continues: The worst pose measured so far: ground level at a hilltop, shadows and AO on, looking out over the terrain. CLAUDE.md records 76 fps here against 155-159 panoramic, so this -- not the panorama -- is the pose a GPU budget is set from. Used by goals 220 and 221 as the instrumentation-cost measurement pose.
backend both

# TAA off for every scenario that compares a capture against a golden. Measured, not assumed:
# with TAA on, vk-vs-vk moves 0.996% of pixels at this pose against a 1.5% gate, and with it off
# 0.341% -- see dev/harness/src/image_compare.hpp for the full four-case table.
option --no-taa
option --cell-log2 5

pose_ground 48,0 -90 -6 1.7
wait 5

capture end grid_stress no-golden

assert frames > 0
assert contrast_percent > 6
